Welcome! I am an Associate Professor at the School of Artificial Intelligence and Computer Science, Xi'an University of Science and Technology (XUST). I received my Ph.D. degree in Computer Application Technology from Northwest University in 2018. My research focuses on IoT sensing, artificial intelligence, crowd computing, and intelligent sensing, with applications to Industrial IoT and coal-mine safety.

== Research Interests

- *IoT Sensing and Mobile Crowdsensing*
- *Artificial Intelligence and Intelligent Perception*
- *Industrial IoT and Coal-Mine Safety Monitoring*

== Recent Publications

- *Jing Zhang*, Ke Huang, Yao Zhang, Bin Guo, Zhiwen Yu, "Detecting Fake Reviewer Groups in Dynamic Networks: An Adaptive Graph Learning Method", /IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering/, vol. 38, no. 5, pp. 2687--2702, 2026.

- *Jing Zhang*, Xingyue Li, Bing Li, Yuguang Xu, Jing Su, "CEA-RPCMLP-HGNN: Point-of-Interest Recommendation Method for City Tourism Crowd", /IEEE Internet of Things Journal/, vol. 13, no. 9, pp. 19006--19017, 2026.

- *Jing Zhang*, Yuqi Chen, Yao Zhang, Bin Guo, Ruonan Xu, "DWHA-PCMSP: Salient Object Detection Network in Coal Mine Industrial IoT", /IEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics/, vol. 21, no. 7, pp. 5746--5754, 2025.

